<p class=3D"xmsonormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:105%"><spa=
n style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:105%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot=
;,sans-serif">Finally, in evaluating a public records request fee waiver th=
e public body must consider whether, under the totality
 of the circumstances, a fee waiver is also in the public interest. When we=
ighing the public interest in disclosure versus the public interest in pres=
erving public funds, when none of the prescribed factors weigh in favor of =
the grant of a fee waiver, the grant
 of a fee waiver is not warranted. Consequently, your request for a fee wai=
ver is denied.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
